P3-5 debug/release/memcheck runtime-stability evidence
Date: 2026-08-26
Branch: feature/hybrid-recall
Validated commit: 4c032d0fb7b4f90f6a05a5f45e23cdaaa29dc096

Scope
  - one QueryDesc executed 100 times with ExecutorRewind between runs
  - 100 real parallel OGAI executions with alternating RRF parameters
  - deterministic statement timeout while both task-stream producers run
  - successful parallel query and instance-liveness check after cancellation
  - isolated clean release and official memcheck builds

Test vehicle changes
  docs/hybrid_recall/p04_test_module/hybrid_recall_test.cpp adds the test-only
  hybrid_recall_debug_rescan entry point.  It constructs one serial
  HybridRecall QueryDesc, calls ExecutorRun, then repeats
  ExecutorRewind -> ExecReScanHybridRecall -> ExecutorRun 99 times.  The
  return value is the total number of emitted rows, so 3 rows * 100 loops
  must equal 300.

  hybrid_recall_debug_parallel now restores the process-wide producer-delay
  hook in PG_CATCH before rethrowing timeout/cancel.  Executor resources
  continue to unwind through the statement ResourceOwner.

  p04_test_module/build.sh checks the rescan symbol and installs a unique
  hybrid_recall_p35_test.so alias so the old pg_plugin library cache cannot
  reuse an earlier test module.

