Memcheck initialization boundary
  The official memcheck gs_initdb executable recursively emitted
  AddressSanitizer:DEADLYSIGNAL even for --version and produced no symbolized
  ASAN report.  The same command works in the older hand-configured ASAN tree;
  this is therefore recorded as an official memcheck utility/runtime boundary,
  not hidden as a successful initdb run.

  Kernel runtime validation used an offline copy of the release PGDATA created
  by the same commit 4c032d0fb7.  The release instance was already stopped;
  the copied data directory was assigned port 55641 and started with the
  current official-memcheck gaussdb.  No user or main-instance PGDATA was used.

Memcheck/ASAN runtime
  ASAN_OPTIONS:
    detect_leaks=0:detect_odr_violation=0:handle_segv=0:
    abort_on_error=1:halt_on_error=1:log_path=/tmp/P3-5_memcheck_server_asan
  Notes:
    detect_odr_violation=0 avoids the documented openGauss client/parser ODR
    duplicate; handle_segv=0 avoids recursive handling between openGauss and
    ASAN.  Address/UAF/double-free/bounds instrumentation remains active.
    Exit-time LSan scanning is disabled for the persistent multithread server;
